WEBVTT

00:08.200 --> 00:12.080
I don't get to take a day off because I don't get paid time off.

00:12.280 --> 00:20.640
I have very minimal sick hours and I have to strategically decide when I might,
in a few months, be sick enough to get a day off.

00:21.440 --> 00:29.720
I only get three days for an entire year — so kind of just making it work.

00:30.520 --> 00:37.520
I don't get the same benefits as my permanent staff and I work probably just as hard as they do,

00:37.520 --> 00:47.360
if not more — and I don't get benefits for my children, otherwise it would be at a very high cost.

00:47.360 --> 00:51.660
I don't get any sick time besides my four days.

00:51.660 --> 00:58.000
I don't have any vacation time, so it's a little unfair.

00:58.000 --> 01:02.600
It's almost a two-tier system.

01:02.600 --> 01:13.260
We're almost like, I would say, modern-day serf workers — because the permanent staff are entitled to all the benefits, whereas extra-help staff are not.

01:13.260 --> 01:18.080
Currently our county has 20% of its workforce as extra-help workers.

01:18.080 --> 01:20.280
That's the highest amount of extra-help staff here in the Bay Area.
